WEBVTT

00:06.589 --> 00:09.551
[sweet airy music]

00:43.001 --> 00:43.877
[Ung] Did you…

00:44.919 --> 00:46.629
also know about it?

00:46.713 --> 00:48.923
Excuse me, what's this about?

00:49.007 --> 00:50.300
Did you know that…

00:52.010 --> 00:54.637
that Nu-a's also
taking part in this project?

00:55.221 --> 00:56.055
I'm asking you, Ms. Kook.

00:56.931 --> 00:58.933
[tense music]

00:59.976 --> 01:02.228
Wait, what do you…

01:04.856 --> 01:08.485
Excuse me, can we just
talk about that matter later?

01:09.360 --> 01:10.278
You see?

01:11.946 --> 01:13.114
It's always been you…

01:15.325 --> 01:16.576
You ruin me.

01:17.160 --> 01:18.161
[shaky breath]

01:19.788 --> 01:22.040
[tense music continues]

01:26.044 --> 01:29.631
[Ji-ung] Everything…
started a long time ago.

01:30.381 --> 01:31.674
YEAR 2000

01:31.758 --> 01:33.092
When we were still kids.

01:33.176 --> 01:34.344
- [kid] It's you, right?
- Hi.

01:34.427 --> 01:36.971
- Hello.
- Doesn't your dad own Ung's Snack Bar?

01:37.055 --> 01:40.058
Come on, tell us what it's like.
Do you eat tteokbokki every single day?

01:40.141 --> 01:41.559
- [boy 1] Can I come?
- [boy 2] Me too!

01:41.643 --> 01:43.436
[Ji-ung] It was all because of our names.

01:43.520 --> 01:44.729
- You got it all wrong.
- What?

01:45.313 --> 01:46.648
My dad doesn't run a snack bar.

01:47.774 --> 01:48.983
[Ung] His does.

01:49.776 --> 01:51.110
[kids shouting excitedly]

01:51.903 --> 01:53.363
"Kim Ji-ung"?

01:53.947 --> 01:56.616
- Oh, so your dad runs Ung's Snack Bar?
- [boy 2] It must be him!

01:56.699 --> 01:59.661
- [boy 3] Hey, I wanna be friends with you!
- [boy 4] So it's yours!

01:59.744 --> 02:02.038
- [boy 2] No, he's my friend.
- Hey! Hey, Choi Ung!

02:02.122 --> 02:05.333
[Ji-ung] I guess our story
was similar to The Prince and the Pauper…

02:05.416 --> 02:06.626
- [boy 4] Let him go.
- [kids whining]

02:06.709 --> 02:07.627
GAMJATANG WITH UNG

02:07.710 --> 02:10.380
…where the prince and the pauper
shared the same name.

02:11.464 --> 02:13.299
- [woman 1] Thanks for the food.
- [woman 2] Sure.

02:15.635 --> 02:16.803
- [Ji-ung] To be honest…
- Hello!

02:16.886 --> 02:19.848
- …why would a kid be envious of that?
- Oh, my, you're so cute. Are you Ung?

02:19.931 --> 02:22.976
Gosh, you're very lucky. You're so young,
but you already have a restaurant.

02:23.059 --> 02:25.562
That's what I thought.
Are you going to take on

02:25.645 --> 02:27.981
- the family business?
- [woman 2] Of course he will.

02:28.064 --> 02:30.275
It makes sense,
since the restaurant is named after him.

02:30.358 --> 02:31.943
[Ji-ung] When you hear those things,

02:32.026 --> 02:34.654
- to a kid, they seem like nonsense.
- [woman 2] You're so lucky, bye.

02:35.280 --> 02:37.323
[soft music]

02:38.241 --> 02:39.117
[Ji-ung] Hey.

02:39.701 --> 02:42.453
What's the matter with you?
Why'd you have to lie like that?

02:44.330 --> 02:45.790
Oh, I'm sorry.

02:47.208 --> 02:49.669
- What are you doing here?
- I'm just sitting here.

02:49.752 --> 02:52.839
But how come you've been
sitting alone outside for hours?

02:52.922 --> 02:55.675
My mom told me to stay put and play here.

02:55.758 --> 02:56.634
Why?

02:57.552 --> 02:59.012
She said it's dangerous.

02:59.846 --> 03:01.514
[Ji-ung] And he seemed a bit pathetic

03:03.099 --> 03:04.392
to be considered a prince.

03:05.977 --> 03:07.520
[chuckles]
Funny, right?

03:08.271 --> 03:09.856
Me feeling sorry for someone.

03:12.275 --> 03:14.819
[gentle piano music]

03:23.870 --> 03:26.080
[gentle piano music continues]

03:30.710 --> 03:31.961
[sighs]

03:37.216 --> 03:38.843
I guess he seemed more lonely…

03:44.557 --> 03:45.892
than pathetic.

03:50.355 --> 03:53.858
WITH UNG

03:58.613 --> 04:00.406
Do you want me to tell you a scary story?

04:04.118 --> 04:05.370
I'm not making this up.

04:05.453 --> 04:07.956
All the events
in this story really happened.

04:08.039 --> 04:11.876
Every night at 12 a.m.,
when the bell rang three times…

04:13.544 --> 04:15.630
I think that's how we became friends.

04:19.092 --> 04:23.096
Although, having a friend
didn't make much of a difference for me.

04:26.975 --> 04:30.728
- I have to go.
- You're leaving to have dinner again?

04:30.812 --> 04:32.313
What are you, a dog?

04:33.606 --> 04:36.067
I had fun today. See you tomorrow.

04:37.026 --> 04:38.152
[sighs]

04:40.488 --> 04:44.075
[Ji-ung] So in the end,
I was left all by myself.

04:47.495 --> 04:49.998
By the way, when is your mom coming home?

04:51.249 --> 04:52.375
[Ji-ung] Really late.

04:52.959 --> 04:55.461
- Why?
- [Ji-ung] Because she's busy working.

04:56.713 --> 04:57.922
What about your dad then?

04:59.299 --> 05:01.009
I don't have a dad.

05:02.969 --> 05:04.971
Since they're not here, who eats with you?

05:10.643 --> 05:11.936
[Yeon-ok] Ta-da.

05:12.645 --> 05:14.188
Go and eat up, Ji-ung.

05:14.272 --> 05:16.899
Thank you, ma'am. Thank you, sir.

05:16.983 --> 05:19.777
Gosh, look at you being so polite.
[chuckles]

05:20.361 --> 05:22.530
Oh, my, you and my son have the same names

05:22.613 --> 05:25.867
and I can tell you're
a polite and smart kid. Right?

05:25.950 --> 05:29.329
- And one, two, three. Ta-da.
- Wow.

05:30.330 --> 05:33.374
- Oh, this is too hot!
- Have dinner with us often, okay?

05:33.958 --> 05:35.960
Thank you for being good friends with Ung.

05:36.586 --> 05:39.589
What do you want, Ung? Some eggs?
Do you want eggs?

05:39.672 --> 05:41.841
[Yeon-ok] I'll give you a lot.
Let's see… Here.

05:41.924 --> 05:43.551
- [Yeon-ok] What about you Ji-ung?
- [Ho] Meat.

05:44.135 --> 05:46.888
- That's right. Some meat. Here you go.
- More meat. Meat it is.

05:46.971 --> 05:49.223
[Ho] That's great. My turn?

05:49.307 --> 05:50.892
- [Yeon-ok] You can get your own.
- [Ho] Okay.

05:50.975 --> 05:53.728
[Ji-ung] I'd never been
so envious of anyone before.

05:53.811 --> 05:54.729
Eat up, go on.

05:55.480 --> 05:58.608
- Mmm. I'll have some garlic rice.
- [Ho] Mmm. Yum.

05:59.942 --> 06:02.278
[Ji-ung] I thought I'd never
be able to have what he had.

06:02.361 --> 06:03.613
Here you go, Ung.

06:03.696 --> 06:05.907
- What?
- Want more?

06:05.990 --> 06:07.617
[teacher] Okay, line up, everyone.

06:07.700 --> 06:09.368
- [teacher] Come forward.
- [Ji-ung] But then…

06:10.119 --> 06:12.705
[kids chatting excitedly]

06:20.171 --> 06:21.672
[Ung] This is for you.

06:23.132 --> 06:25.009
[Ji-ung] Choi Ung
didn't feel the same way.

06:28.137 --> 06:29.138
Are you done already?

06:29.222 --> 06:30.431
Thank you for the food, ma'am.

06:30.515 --> 06:33.309
Oh, gosh, you're so adorable
when you're polite.

06:33.392 --> 06:34.685
[chuckles]
Finish your food.

06:34.769 --> 06:36.687
I heard you boys are going bike riding.

06:36.771 --> 06:39.357
[staff] Excuse me, ma'am.
Could you take a look at this please?

06:39.440 --> 06:41.192
Coming! I'll be back.

06:41.275 --> 06:43.277
- Eat up and have some bananas.
- Okay.

06:49.242 --> 06:51.160
Can you eat some of this for me?

06:54.872 --> 06:57.083
[upbeat music]

06:59.252 --> 07:00.920
[Ji-ung] Choi Ung shared
everything with me

07:01.003 --> 07:02.797
like it was a natural thing to do.

07:03.297 --> 07:05.967
[bright cheery music]

07:13.307 --> 07:15.184
- You wanna bet?
- Oh, okay!

07:15.268 --> 07:16.978
- Seriously?
- [both chuckle]

07:20.690 --> 07:22.275
[Ji-ung] His time…

07:25.528 --> 07:27.155
Come on. That's cheating.

07:27.238 --> 07:28.239
[brakes squeal]

07:28.948 --> 07:31.534
[Ji-ung] I told you,
you can't beat me. I win!

07:31.617 --> 07:32.994
Hey, dad, let me help you.

07:33.077 --> 07:34.287
No, it's okay.

07:34.370 --> 07:36.914
- [Ji-ung] No, let me carry it for you.
- It's okay, Ji-ung. I can manage.

07:36.998 --> 07:39.292
- [Ji-ung] No, really, I insist.
- [Ho] Put it down. It's heavy.

07:39.375 --> 07:42.003
Hey, Choi Ung. Where are you going?
Aren't you gonna help out?

07:42.587 --> 07:43.880
But Ji-ung is stronger.

07:43.963 --> 07:45.840
- [Ho] So many excuses…
- [Ji-ung] …his daily life…

07:45.923 --> 07:47.091
[Ho] Then Ji-ung, could you please…

07:47.175 --> 07:50.928
- [Ji-ung] Everyone ready? One, two, three.
- [shutter clicks]

07:52.221 --> 07:53.639
Hey, come over.

07:53.723 --> 07:56.684
- Yes. Come here, Ji-ung. Hurry up!
- Oh, could you take our picture, please?

07:56.767 --> 07:58.227
[Ho] Come over here, Ji-ung.

07:58.311 --> 07:59.187
There.

07:59.270 --> 08:02.356
Excuse me, sir, please make sure
my two sons look good in the photo.

08:02.440 --> 08:03.566
CONGRATULATIONS ON YOUR GRADUATION

08:05.193 --> 08:06.235
Look, look.

08:06.319 --> 08:08.613
- [Ji-ung] …and even his family.
- [Ho] Smile for the camera!

08:08.696 --> 08:10.781
- Go on, smile for the camera.
- [man] One, two, three.

08:11.616 --> 08:13.201
[Ji-ung] Thanks to him, I was able

08:13.284 --> 08:16.412
to experience happiness
by inserting myself into his life.

08:17.413 --> 08:18.831
[students chatting]

08:24.337 --> 08:28.466
But in these stories, there's always
another character that comes in.

08:28.549 --> 08:30.551
[soft music]

08:42.939 --> 08:45.983
It's obvious. It's so obvious, but…

08:47.693 --> 08:50.196
[soft music continues]

09:04.710 --> 09:06.170
Looks like you need this.

09:16.138 --> 09:16.973
Do you

09:18.307 --> 09:19.308
need it back?

09:20.726 --> 09:22.937
- You can keep it.
- Thank you.

09:27.567 --> 09:29.318
[Ji-ung] She was incredibly pretty.

09:32.071 --> 09:34.323
HWIYEONG HIGH SCHOOL
ENTRANCE CEREMONY

09:34.407 --> 09:35.616
[applause]

09:37.535 --> 09:40.329
[teacher] Next, the principal will give
a welcoming speech

09:40.413 --> 09:42.081
to formally open the school year.

09:43.291 --> 09:45.418
[principal] I know a lot of you
are excited for spring.

09:45.501 --> 09:49.255
I would like to thank all of you
for being here despite the cold weather.

09:49.338 --> 09:53.259
I would like to thank you all
for being here on this very special day.

09:53.968 --> 09:55.469
Seeing all of you here…

09:56.512 --> 09:58.347
[soft music]

09:59.265 --> 10:00.558
[Ji-ung] But the problem was…

10:01.100 --> 10:03.561
I wasn't the only one who thought so.

10:05.396 --> 10:07.023
That, right there, was the twist.

10:07.773 --> 10:11.444
I told myself… it wasn't a problem.

10:11.527 --> 10:13.112
[sighs deeply]

10:13.195 --> 10:14.947
[rain clattering]

10:24.415 --> 10:25.541
I knew then…

10:28.085 --> 10:31.255
what I had to do was take a step back.

10:32.423 --> 10:34.800
[somber piano music]

10:35.926 --> 10:37.595
You see, I know that…

10:38.471 --> 10:40.973
I'm not the main character in this story.

10:42.433 --> 10:43.851
We can wrap up for tonight.

10:43.934 --> 10:44.935
Thanks, see you.

10:47.146 --> 10:49.565
A SECRET THAT CAN'T BE TOLD

10:49.649 --> 10:53.361
EPISODE 5

10:54.612 --> 10:55.946
[inhales]

10:56.030 --> 10:58.616
Things got
more complicated than I thought.

10:59.283 --> 11:00.368
[sighs]

11:00.951 --> 11:04.121
- Excuse me, Mr. Jang.
- Yes, what is it, Ms. Kook?

11:04.205 --> 11:05.831
What did he mean a while ago?

11:05.915 --> 11:09.126
Why did he say
Nu-a will be participating in the project?

11:09.210 --> 11:10.127
You heard what he said.

11:10.211 --> 11:13.130
I showed you in my reports
that the plagiarism accusation was false.

11:13.214 --> 11:15.049
- So how could you--
- One second.

11:16.467 --> 11:18.594
Please take our guest to the other room.

11:18.677 --> 11:19.720
[in French]
Excuse me.

11:24.183 --> 11:26.811
Tell me, what is the one thing
we need the most right now?

11:29.230 --> 11:30.398
An issue.

11:30.898 --> 11:32.817
Right now, I think this is
the best way for the brand--

11:32.900 --> 11:35.736
But this decision
is clearly a breach of contract,

11:35.820 --> 11:37.363
and it's disrespectful to the artist--

11:37.446 --> 11:40.157
You see, I'm not so sure about that.
I already checked the contract,

11:40.241 --> 11:41.867
and there seemed to be no problem.

11:42.660 --> 11:44.787
Disrespectful…
[inhales]

11:44.870 --> 11:47.206
You're being unusually emotional.

11:47.289 --> 11:50.835
You must admit, this could be
a great opportunity for both artists.

11:50.918 --> 11:53.254
[Do-yul] So why are you
making it into a big deal?

11:53.337 --> 11:55.589
[dramatic music]

11:59.969 --> 12:01.178
[sighs]

12:02.847 --> 12:04.515
You disappoint me.

12:04.598 --> 12:08.185
In the beginning, I thought you'd be
rational enough to see this event through.

12:08.269 --> 12:12.189
But I guess, you can't keep
private matters separate from work.

12:15.317 --> 12:17.278
Anyway then, let's have
a meeting about his later--

12:17.361 --> 12:20.406
You, sir, are going to have to apologize.

12:20.489 --> 12:23.784
- Pardon?
- You heard me loud and clear, Mr. Jang.

12:23.868 --> 12:26.704
You will clear this up
by apologizing to Mr. Choi.

12:27.496 --> 12:29.415
- Ms. Kook.
- I'm not being emotional.

12:29.498 --> 12:30.416
I'm being empathetic.

12:31.000 --> 12:34.420
Being good at your job without empathy
isn't something to be proud of.

12:34.503 --> 12:36.630
[Yeon-su] Empathy is linked
to intelligence.

12:36.714 --> 12:38.716
You lack respect in the artists,

12:38.799 --> 12:42.011
and you showed
you have no value for their art, Mr. Jang.

12:42.094 --> 12:44.805
You have to meet Mr. Choi
to apologize to him

12:44.889 --> 12:46.599
about everything that happened today.

12:46.682 --> 12:49.894
And as the person in charge,
I'll take care of the consequences.

12:49.977 --> 12:52.813
I seriously hope
you haven't planned any more surprises.

12:57.026 --> 13:00.279
I can't believe you entertained the idea
that I was anything like you.

13:01.113 --> 13:03.908
Now I'm taking a second look
at my past actions.

13:03.991 --> 13:06.076
[dramatic music continues]

13:07.870 --> 13:09.955
- Wow.
- What do we do? Should we follow her?

13:10.039 --> 13:12.917
- We should just go. It's all over now.
- Oh.

13:13.000 --> 13:14.376
[music fades]

13:22.468 --> 13:24.136
[Ji-ung] Ung has always been this way.

13:25.346 --> 13:26.680
Are you okay?

13:28.015 --> 13:28.974
Mm-hmm.

13:29.058 --> 13:31.435
[Ji-ung] He's always been
so quiet and calm.

13:32.061 --> 13:35.814
But whenever Yeon-su appears,
his whole stoic demeanor would shatter.

13:36.815 --> 13:38.567
The Choi Ung I knew back then,

13:39.443 --> 13:42.029
now that guy
was the picture of absolute calm.

13:42.112 --> 13:44.615
[guys yelling instructions]

13:44.698 --> 13:46.200
- [guy 1] Shoot!
- [guy 2] I'm open!

13:46.283 --> 13:48.077
- [guy 3] Nice.
- [guy 4] Let's rest for a bit.

13:48.869 --> 13:50.788
[indistinct chatter]

13:52.248 --> 13:55.501
Hey, Ung, will you take a break
and shoot some hoops with us?

13:56.085 --> 13:57.086
[guy 3] Come on.

13:58.462 --> 14:01.382
[Ji-ung] He had no interest
in what was going on around him.

14:01.465 --> 14:03.175
[sighs]
Here.

14:05.010 --> 14:07.179
- Look, it's Kook Yeon-su.
- [guy 3] Who's that?

14:07.263 --> 14:09.348
[guy 4] The girl who entered
with the highest scores.

14:09.848 --> 14:12.059
She's pretty, but I hear she's rude.

14:14.103 --> 14:16.438
[soft music]

14:21.443 --> 14:23.904
[Ji-ung] He only became aware
when Kook Yeon-su appeared.

14:26.448 --> 14:28.826
[soft music continues]

14:32.121 --> 14:33.122
[sighs]

14:35.040 --> 14:36.834
I know it may sound weird,

14:36.917 --> 14:40.504
but I always thought
Choi Ung and I were very similar

14:40.588 --> 14:43.591
in that usually none of our emotions
would show on our faces.

14:43.674 --> 14:45.593
[rapid knocking]

14:47.469 --> 14:49.471
[panting]

14:49.555 --> 14:51.140
Until the day everything changed.

14:51.223 --> 14:53.434
Ji-ung, I got a girlfriend.

14:54.768 --> 14:57.438
- [light music]
- [chuckles]

15:00.649 --> 15:01.817
You broke up again?

15:02.735 --> 15:03.903
[Ji-ung] If it's Kook Yeon-su,

15:03.986 --> 15:06.280
even the smallest things
would drive him crazy.

15:07.156 --> 15:08.282
[sighs]

15:08.908 --> 15:11.660
How many times has it been?
Five times? Six?

15:13.412 --> 15:15.497
Don't you think
you're being overly dramatic?

15:16.290 --> 15:19.168
Get used to it.
You break up every two minutes anyway.

15:21.837 --> 15:23.964
[light music continues]

15:27.009 --> 15:30.554
He became an immature guy
with no control over his emotions.

15:32.264 --> 15:34.350
[soft pensive music]

15:36.769 --> 15:37.811
Hey.

15:40.606 --> 15:42.691
We'll talk later. Never mind.

15:42.775 --> 15:43.651
[music stops]

15:46.111 --> 15:47.154
[Ji-ung inhales]

15:49.239 --> 15:51.116
[engine starts]

15:51.200 --> 15:53.035
[engine revs]

15:57.373 --> 15:58.791
Hey, I'm home.

15:59.375 --> 16:03.295
Oh, you're back so early.
I thought you'd be out all night.

16:03.379 --> 16:05.297
If you did,
you shouldn't be waiting for me.

16:05.381 --> 16:07.925
- What are you doing outside?
- [chuckles]

16:08.008 --> 16:11.387
I have to sure my baby's safe
before I sleep.

16:11.470 --> 16:16.517
Oh, look at you, my granddaughter's
so pretty wearing that dress.

16:16.600 --> 16:19.269
Your granddaughter looks pretty
wearing regular clothes too.

16:19.353 --> 16:21.313
- [chuckles]
- Oh, my. What were you doing?

16:21.397 --> 16:23.482
- I wasn't doing anything special.
- [sighs]

16:24.274 --> 16:28.112
- So tell me, how did your party go?
- [inhales]

16:28.195 --> 16:30.656
It was great.
All the guests looked so cool.

16:30.739 --> 16:33.701
They were all dressed up
as if they were born like that.

16:33.784 --> 16:34.702
[soft chuckle]

16:35.577 --> 16:38.664
[pensive music]

16:43.544 --> 16:45.337
Hang on, grandma, were you alone all day?

16:45.421 --> 16:48.257
What? Oh, well, yes, I was.

16:49.466 --> 16:52.720
How come grandma Ji-na
hasn't been visiting you these days?

16:53.804 --> 16:55.597
She's probably just busy.

16:56.181 --> 16:57.599
Did you have a fight with her?

16:57.683 --> 16:59.309
I didn't start it, no.

17:01.061 --> 17:03.856
That woman wouldn't stop nagging me,
she kept saying nonsense.

17:03.939 --> 17:06.900
That's why I had to set her straight,
but it wasn't exactly a fight.

17:06.984 --> 17:08.569
I bet you picked that fight with her.

17:08.652 --> 17:10.279
You must have said mean things
and ended up

17:10.362 --> 17:12.573
hurting grandma Ji-na's
feelings again, didn't you?

17:12.656 --> 17:14.533
I didn't! How could you?

17:14.616 --> 17:18.162
Now, go get washed up and go to sleep.
Stop talking nonsense.

17:18.245 --> 17:20.956
I can't believe
how our personalities are so similar.

17:21.040 --> 17:23.333
Can't you be more patient
and get along with her?

17:27.004 --> 17:28.839
You should go see grandma Ji-na tomorrow.

17:28.922 --> 17:31.633
- I'm never doing that.
- [Yeon-su] Fine, then I'll bring her here.

17:31.717 --> 17:36.055
Mind your own business.
She'll probably say no.

17:37.848 --> 17:40.350
Stop being so stubborn
and apologize to her.

17:41.894 --> 17:44.855
[soft pensive music]

17:54.156 --> 17:56.158
[clears throat]

17:58.202 --> 18:00.329
Stop being so stubborn
and apologize to me.

18:01.538 --> 18:02.790
For what?

18:03.916 --> 18:07.211
Come on, you know what you did wrong,
that's why you owe me an apology.

18:08.087 --> 18:10.881
[Ung] I get it,
you couldn't call me first or come see me.

18:12.049 --> 18:13.926
It's your pride that was holding you back.

18:14.843 --> 18:17.096
My guess is,
you've been thinking the entire day

18:17.179 --> 18:18.305
about what you could've done.

18:20.224 --> 18:21.433
Who? Me?

18:21.517 --> 18:23.811
[inhales]
That's the reason why I'm here now.

18:24.394 --> 18:26.063
Now's your chance. Apologize.

18:32.778 --> 18:34.488
[awkward tune]

18:44.039 --> 18:45.791
[awkward tune continues]

18:58.470 --> 19:00.514
How hard could it be to say sorry?

19:03.684 --> 19:05.686
It's hard. I don't do it so often.

19:05.769 --> 19:08.272
Then start practicing from now on.

19:08.355 --> 19:10.774
But if I do that,
everyone will look down on me.

19:10.858 --> 19:11.942
I hate losing.

19:12.651 --> 19:13.735
[sighs]

19:14.278 --> 19:15.112
Fine, I'll go.

19:22.327 --> 19:23.620
Sorry.

19:25.455 --> 19:26.999
I made a mistake.

19:29.835 --> 19:31.587
What was that? I can't hear you.

19:33.130 --> 19:37.050
I said sorry! So… don't go…

19:37.134 --> 19:38.510
[Ung chuckles softly]

19:42.264 --> 19:45.017
You idiot. It can be like that with me.

19:46.268 --> 19:48.562
You know that
I'll keep coming back to you.

19:48.645 --> 19:50.647
But you also gotta learn to apologize.

19:52.024 --> 19:53.609
I'll always give in anyway.

19:56.737 --> 19:57.738
[chuckles softly]

19:58.947 --> 20:00.991
[gentle music]

20:04.453 --> 20:06.371
[Yeon-su] He must be furious with me.

20:08.248 --> 20:11.043
He'll probably
be bottling everything up inside.

20:12.920 --> 20:15.172
["Summer Rain" by Sam Kim playing]

20:49.998 --> 20:52.417
["Summer Rain" by Sam Kim continues]

21:07.683 --> 21:09.101
[deep sigh]

21:13.480 --> 21:15.148
[music fades]

21:17.651 --> 21:19.403
[Chae-ran] Are you planning
to go somewhere?

21:19.486 --> 21:22.489
Oh, well, there's something
I need to take care of,

21:22.572 --> 21:24.491
so I'll swing by Ung's place to see him.

21:24.574 --> 21:27.911
Something happened yesterday,
so I need to apologize.

21:27.995 --> 21:30.956
It's not like I did something wrong.
No, it wasn't my fault.

21:31.039 --> 21:32.666
It's just a misunderstanding.

21:32.749 --> 21:35.085
But, looking back, if I were in his shoes,

21:35.168 --> 21:36.962
I'm pretty sure I'd be feeling upset.

21:37.045 --> 21:40.507
Which is why
I'm going to talk to him right away.

21:41.508 --> 21:43.510
He's usually at home anyway.

21:43.593 --> 21:45.345
[Chae-ran] You talked to him on the phone?

21:45.971 --> 21:49.975
Um, I tried calling him yesterday,
but I think he was asleep.

21:50.058 --> 21:51.435
I'll just call him again.

21:53.937 --> 21:55.188
[dial tone]

21:55.939 --> 21:58.025
But just to be clear,
none of this was my fault.

21:58.108 --> 21:59.109
I wasn't doing anything.

21:59.192 --> 22:01.403
In fact, he was the one
who was jumping to conclusions.

22:01.486 --> 22:04.990
Unbelievable. Does he really think
I'd be capable of such a thing?

22:05.991 --> 22:07.409
[dial tone]

22:09.494 --> 22:11.204
Speaking of, when Choi Ung
made that comment

22:11.288 --> 22:12.748
about how I always ruin his life,

22:12.831 --> 22:14.624
that was a bit harsh,
don't you think? Right?

22:14.708 --> 22:17.294
Let's face it,
how in the world did I screw up his life?

22:17.377 --> 22:19.629
- [dial tone]
- [sighs]

22:19.713 --> 22:23.300
[operator] The person you are calling
is unavailable. Please try or call…

22:25.469 --> 22:28.889
On that note, there's really no reason
for me to go him, correct?

22:28.972 --> 22:30.223
[Yeon-su] Hm?

22:30.307 --> 22:33.894
I can just sort everything out
and call him later, right?

22:34.978 --> 22:36.521
I've changed my mind. I'm not going.

22:37.022 --> 22:38.440
[Sol-i] Hey!

22:38.523 --> 22:40.358
Kook Yeon-su!

22:42.360 --> 22:44.905
You know, I find it very strange…

22:44.988 --> 22:48.533
that it's normal for the house to be quiet
when you're living on your own.

22:48.617 --> 22:52.913
But I gotta be honest,
now I find the silence a bit unsettling.

22:53.914 --> 22:55.123
[Eun-ho] Ung!

22:55.874 --> 22:57.959
Except for that noise.
I've gotten used to that.

22:59.294 --> 23:00.378
[sighs]

23:02.464 --> 23:03.799
Good morning.

23:06.176 --> 23:08.804
Ung, I heard about
what happened yesterday.

23:08.887 --> 23:10.514
Good, it's about time.

23:10.597 --> 23:12.432
But how the hell did that happen, Ung?

23:12.516 --> 23:14.476
Tell me about it.
I couldn't believe it either.

23:15.060 --> 23:16.478
You went to a party without me?

23:17.604 --> 23:19.815
You got invited
but didn't bother to take me.

23:19.898 --> 23:21.024
You knew I didn't have any plans,

23:21.108 --> 23:23.110
and I was just staying home
watching TV all day.

23:23.193 --> 23:25.987
How could you go to a party all alone,
dressed up like a penguin?

23:26.071 --> 23:27.614
- Stop bitching about it.
- Hey!

23:27.697 --> 23:29.658
You heard about the party,
so you heard about what happened.

23:30.242 --> 23:31.743
Shouldn't you ask me if I'm okay?

23:31.827 --> 23:32.661
What do you mean?

23:32.744 --> 23:35.122
You don't know what happened?
They hired Nu-a. I got screwed.

23:35.205 --> 23:37.624
Oh, that one?
I think it's not that bad, actually.

23:37.707 --> 23:40.794
When you two push through with
the drawing show, you can show your talent

23:40.877 --> 23:43.171
and prove the plagiarism charges
are nothing but lies.

23:43.255 --> 23:44.881
- It'll be good for all of us.
- What?

23:44.965 --> 23:47.175
Of course, I didn't tell
any of them what I thought.

23:47.259 --> 23:49.302
But I made sure to cause
a ruckus when I went there.

23:49.803 --> 23:52.139
"How could you do this to us?
How could you stab us in the back?

23:52.222 --> 23:54.349
We thought so hard about this
before deciding to do it.

23:54.432 --> 23:55.600
This is unacceptable."

23:55.684 --> 23:58.687
That's exactly what I told them
in a very cold and professional way.

23:58.770 --> 24:00.564
Oh.

24:00.647 --> 24:02.732
Yes, I'm pretty good as a manager.

24:03.441 --> 24:05.569
I do my job well.
[chuckles]

24:06.653 --> 24:08.155
Focus on me.

24:09.239 --> 24:10.991
Anyway, we can think about it some more.

24:11.074 --> 24:12.242
You're great at what you do.

24:12.325 --> 24:14.327
And now that you're ready
to show yourself in public,

24:14.411 --> 24:16.371
we can publicly humiliate that small fry.

24:22.252 --> 24:23.336
Listen, Ung.

24:23.837 --> 24:28.216
Have you considered maybe showing
the cameras something more artistic?

24:29.050 --> 24:30.927
- Huh?
- You know what I mean.

24:31.011 --> 24:34.097
If the viewers see this, they'll think
you don't do anything worthwhile,

24:34.181 --> 24:36.224
and that throughout the day
you just eat and sleep.

24:36.308 --> 24:38.059
Show them how much
of a professional you are.

24:38.143 --> 24:39.853
Don't you think
that would be better content?

24:39.936 --> 24:41.771
Hey, wait. I don't like that.

24:41.855 --> 24:43.899
You know I hate
pretentious and fake people.

24:44.608 --> 24:47.068
[Ung] Documentaries are
about showing yourself as it is.

24:47.152 --> 24:49.321
I would really hate to do things
I wouldn't normally do

24:49.404 --> 24:51.239
just because I'm in front of a camera.

24:51.323 --> 24:53.116
Hey! Don't expect me
to be all pretentious.

24:53.200 --> 24:54.826
I won't do it. You can't make me.

24:58.371 --> 24:59.497
Whenever I have time,

24:59.581 --> 25:01.791
I go to the museum
to see various artworks.

25:01.875 --> 25:04.419
Constant stimulation and inspiration,

25:05.462 --> 25:08.215
it's quite important
to people like myself.

25:10.175 --> 25:12.594
I'm sure the video filmed ten years ago

25:12.677 --> 25:14.512
never showed this other side of me.

25:15.138 --> 25:17.474
Hmm. How do I put this…

25:17.557 --> 25:20.310
The fact is, the Korean education style

25:20.393 --> 25:23.813
of road learning,
plus the standardized education,

25:23.897 --> 25:27.817
made it hard for me to show off my talent.

25:27.901 --> 25:30.070
[chuckles softly]
What I'm trying to say is,

25:30.153 --> 25:31.738
this is the real Choi Ung.

25:33.156 --> 25:34.741
- We're done.
- [Ung] Hmm?

25:34.824 --> 25:36.284
Sorry. It ran out of battery.

25:37.661 --> 25:38.828
What? You didn't get that?

25:38.912 --> 25:40.789
Well, I'm gonna go change them.

25:41.790 --> 25:45.043
Hey. This is what you should be shooting,
not the useless crap this morning.

25:45.627 --> 25:47.254
Guess the camera doesn't wanna film you.

25:47.337 --> 25:49.673
- Oh, did the camera throw up? You okay?
- Do you wanna die?

25:49.756 --> 25:52.175
- I'll run out to my car and get it.
- Give me the keys, I'll go get it.

25:52.259 --> 25:55.053
- You just need batteries, right?
- [Ji-ung] Thanks.

25:55.136 --> 25:56.471
- [Eun-ho] Hold on.
- Man.

26:00.100 --> 26:01.351
[phone buzzing]

26:04.437 --> 26:06.398
[buzzing continues]

26:08.566 --> 26:11.653
[Ji-ung] Of course,
I know that none of this is my business.

26:11.736 --> 26:13.113
So has Yeon-su called you?

26:14.990 --> 26:15.991
Why?

26:16.658 --> 26:17.867
Well, after what happened,

26:17.951 --> 26:20.161
don't you think you two
should meet and talk?

26:20.245 --> 26:21.955
[scoffs]
I'll take care of it.

26:22.539 --> 26:24.457
All right, I think you have a plan.

26:24.541 --> 26:28.211
But whatever it is,
do it in front of the camera.

26:29.421 --> 26:31.798
You really are milking this, aren't you?

26:32.507 --> 26:33.425
Forget it.

26:35.093 --> 26:36.428
[sighs]

26:41.141 --> 26:42.142
[Ji-ung sighs]

26:43.643 --> 26:45.270
[Ji-ung] I know I shouldn't meddle.

26:45.353 --> 26:47.230
She's only avoiding you
because she's sorry.

26:49.232 --> 26:51.484
- What?
- The live drawing,

26:51.568 --> 26:53.028
had nothing to do with it.

26:53.611 --> 26:56.698
[Ji-ung] You're not the kind of guy
who'd get upset over that. Or are you?

26:57.782 --> 26:58.908
What are you talking about?

26:58.992 --> 27:01.411
You got mad at her,
and it had nothing to do with work.

27:02.203 --> 27:03.663
You probably know that Yeon-su

27:03.747 --> 27:05.540
wouldn't have signed
the other guy on purpose.

27:08.501 --> 27:10.712
You were taking your anger
out on her for the past.

27:12.505 --> 27:14.507
[Ji-ung] I didn't have to say any of that.

27:14.591 --> 27:16.718
I can tell you still have…

27:18.178 --> 27:19.596
feelings for her.

27:22.474 --> 27:24.351
What answer did I want to hear from him?

27:25.435 --> 27:27.520
[tense music]

27:29.147 --> 27:31.191
Why are you suddenly
so interested in this?

27:32.150 --> 27:34.152
I know it's not
because of the documentary.

27:35.487 --> 27:37.072
I don't think it's so sudden.

27:38.323 --> 27:39.282
Tell me, what do you know?

27:40.408 --> 27:42.243
The question is, what don't I know?

27:44.621 --> 27:46.164
[Ji-ung] What is it
that I wanted to check?

27:47.123 --> 27:48.958
- [phone buzzing]
- [sighs]

27:50.960 --> 27:52.295
[buzzing continues]

27:54.089 --> 27:56.007
[Sol-i cheers]

27:56.966 --> 27:58.468
This is actually perfect.

27:58.551 --> 27:59.969
There's a group reservation today,

28:00.053 --> 28:02.347
so I've been so busy
with all the preparations.

28:02.430 --> 28:05.558
I told you to hire more people.
How will you do this by yourself?

28:05.642 --> 28:07.560
What? Are you volunteering
to pay them for me?

28:07.644 --> 28:11.231
So stop sitting around and help me!
It is your day off.

28:11.815 --> 28:13.858
You're seriously
making me work on my day off?

28:13.942 --> 28:16.152
I'm busy too, shooting a documentary.

28:18.238 --> 28:20.990
Don't you guys want to film her working?

28:21.074 --> 28:22.909
It's a natural thing for her to do.

28:22.992 --> 28:25.203
You're gonna shoot her here anyway, right?

28:25.286 --> 28:26.830
Pretend we're not even around.

28:26.913 --> 28:28.998
[Yeon-su] What do you know
about documentaries?

28:29.082 --> 28:30.125
What's that anyway?

28:37.048 --> 28:38.133
No way.

28:39.300 --> 28:40.135
Octopus?

28:40.218 --> 28:42.720
Special delivery from Mokpo this morning.

28:43.304 --> 28:46.391
I'll set aside a plate of sliced,
raw octopus for you. Deal?

28:47.434 --> 28:49.018
- [inhales]
- [plastic rustles]

28:49.102 --> 28:50.019
So what do I do?

28:50.103 --> 28:52.647
Yeon-su and I have known each other
for about ten years.

28:52.731 --> 28:54.691
We met when we were in college.

28:54.774 --> 28:57.819
As you all know, sometimes
she can be a bit crazy and dramatic.

28:57.902 --> 29:00.113
The two of us became real close
after a huge fight.

29:00.196 --> 29:03.116
But that's in the past. I'm super nice
and get along well with crazy people.

29:03.199 --> 29:05.368
Wait, excuse me.
Don't tell me you're recording her?

29:05.452 --> 29:07.537
You know, I was a big fan of that video.

29:07.620 --> 29:09.164
I wrote a lot in the comment section.

29:09.247 --> 29:10.498
My nickname is "Writer Lee."

29:10.582 --> 29:11.624
Oh, yes, that's me.

29:11.708 --> 29:15.712
- I used to write scripts for TV shows.
- You're supposed to be filming me, there.

29:15.795 --> 29:17.922
Have you heard of the show
Omniscient Psychopath?

29:18.006 --> 29:19.549
I was actually the one who wrote it.

29:19.632 --> 29:23.386
And because I worked hard, I opened
this bar with the money I earned from it.

29:23.470 --> 29:25.597
When I started, I used to have a partner.

29:25.680 --> 29:28.141
[Sol-i] Actually, my partner
was my boyfriend back then.

29:28.224 --> 29:30.435
They never asked to hear your life story.

29:30.518 --> 29:33.855
On the day that I deposited the premium,
I caught him cheating on me.

29:33.938 --> 29:36.649
You asshole.
You shouldn't have gotten caught.

29:36.733 --> 29:38.485
I cut all ties with him and…

29:38.568 --> 29:41.029
through sheer will,
I opened the bar by myself.

29:41.112 --> 29:43.323
Again, no one wants to hear your stories.

29:43.406 --> 29:45.742
Do you think that asshole is
watching right now?

29:46.451 --> 29:48.828
Hey Jin-seob, do you see this?

29:48.912 --> 29:51.623
A group of ten people
made a reservation today.

29:51.706 --> 29:54.417
[Sol-i] I'm doing just fine.
I hope you are too.

29:54.501 --> 29:57.504
Right. Would you mind
sharing with us how you know Choi Ung?

29:58.004 --> 30:01.257
Oh, sure. I know him very well.
When they were in college--

30:01.341 --> 30:04.677
Why do you have too many onions here?
What is this, a Chinese restaurant?

30:04.761 --> 30:06.805
Ma'am, if you wanna
know anything, ask away.

30:06.888 --> 30:09.390
I'll even do an interview
as long as you take great shots of my bar!

30:09.474 --> 30:11.935
- [Eun-ho] Hey. Here you go.
- Thanks.

30:13.061 --> 30:14.145
Where did Ung go?

30:15.855 --> 30:18.942
- Something came up, so he left.
- What? What happened?

30:19.025 --> 30:21.611
Didn't he say anything else?
Wait, he just left me here?

30:21.694 --> 30:23.488
Well, he left me here too.

30:23.571 --> 30:26.407
Gosh. He has been acting crazy these days.

30:26.491 --> 30:29.828
This won't do. As his manager,
I'll give him a piece of my mind.

30:30.662 --> 30:31.830
So, where are you off to now?

30:31.913 --> 30:33.998
- [phone buzzing]
- I was… Hold on a sec.

30:39.295 --> 30:41.172
Hey, what's up? Why'd you call?

30:42.966 --> 30:45.426
Right now? Today?

30:46.845 --> 30:49.055
Was it too much to give me
even an hour's notice?

30:50.557 --> 30:52.559
[sighs]
Just send the assistant director.

30:52.642 --> 30:54.102
No, you can't get Chae-ran.

30:56.604 --> 30:58.648
[sighs]
Okay, fine. I'll go.

30:58.731 --> 31:01.276
Hey, wait a minute.
The camera crew is coming too, right?

31:02.193 --> 31:03.027
Okay, bye.

31:04.320 --> 31:06.948
- Are they making you shoot something else?
- Yes, I gotta go, bye.

31:07.031 --> 31:08.741
Wait… Ji-ung.
[sighs]

31:09.951 --> 31:11.953
Hey, bro, I know you're working right now,

31:12.036 --> 31:14.330
but can you drop me off first
before you go there?

31:15.498 --> 31:18.918
Remember, we're filming a documentary.
He's the director.

31:19.002 --> 31:21.004
Hello. Give it to her.

31:22.088 --> 31:23.047
Yes.

31:24.591 --> 31:26.926
[Ji-ung] To give you a better idea,
we're shooting a video

31:27.010 --> 31:29.262
for the 700th episode.
It's going to be for a special.

31:29.345 --> 31:32.140
You just have to say congratulations
and a simple greeting to the viewers

31:32.223 --> 31:33.266
and that's basically it.

31:33.349 --> 31:34.934
Is the producer coming to the shoot?

31:35.018 --> 31:36.644
He's not. I'll take care of everything.

31:37.562 --> 31:38.563
Oh.

31:38.646 --> 31:40.982
The camera's set up,
and we're good, so we'll start shooting

31:41.065 --> 31:42.525
as soon as you're ready to go.

31:43.484 --> 31:44.736
Excuse me.

31:46.154 --> 31:47.864
Haven't we met before?

31:49.866 --> 31:51.910
- Me?
- Don't you know me?

31:53.369 --> 31:55.914
- Everyone knows who you are.
- Not like that.

31:55.997 --> 31:58.207
When I filmed this four years ago,
you were working

31:58.291 --> 32:00.793
as the assistant director,
if I remember correctly.

32:00.877 --> 32:03.379
- Oh, yes. That's right.
- I knew it.

32:03.463 --> 32:06.591
How come you pretended not to know me
and gave me the cold shoulder?

32:06.674 --> 32:08.593
I wasn't sure if you'd remembered me.

32:08.676 --> 32:11.179
[chuckles]
My memory's great. I remember everything.

32:11.262 --> 32:12.680
Thank you for remembering.

32:13.389 --> 32:17.101
I was very young, so I was so clumsy,
and I felt so stupid back then.

32:17.185 --> 32:19.228
But you were
standing in the corner looking lost too.

32:19.312 --> 32:21.773
[chuckles]
You ended up comforting me a lot.

32:21.856 --> 32:25.360
You can talk about the video naturally
just like you did now, that would work.

32:25.443 --> 32:27.987
But, I don't remember much from before.

32:28.071 --> 32:31.824
My schedule was pretty crazy back then
and a lot of cameras were pointed at me.

32:31.908 --> 32:34.285
It was so hectic, I didn't even know
which company was which.

32:34.369 --> 32:37.538
What I do remember,
was when we had gotten to the part

32:37.622 --> 32:39.082
of the shoot where I was meditating.

32:39.165 --> 32:41.876
You were in the corner with a kettle,
you dozed off and you dropped it.

32:41.960 --> 32:43.628
- You got scolded so badly.
- [chuckles]

32:43.711 --> 32:45.755
[NJ] I was actually half-asleep
when I was meditating.

32:45.838 --> 32:48.257
I was tired, so I lied
when I said that's what I was doing.

32:49.467 --> 32:51.844
The sound of the kettle hitting the floor
really woke me up.

32:51.928 --> 32:53.388
[awkward chuckle]

32:53.471 --> 32:55.139
How about we talk
about something else then?

32:55.723 --> 32:58.351
You're different now.
Seems like you've changed a lot, director.

32:59.936 --> 33:02.105
What kind of programs
are you filming these days?

33:02.188 --> 33:03.773
Looks to me like
you're the one in charge now.

33:03.856 --> 33:06.275
Right now,
I'm focusing on doing a special.

33:06.859 --> 33:09.404
Oh, another one. So what is it about?

33:12.115 --> 33:14.659
Sliced raw octopus
that looks just like you.

33:16.703 --> 33:18.162
Now that I think about it,

33:18.246 --> 33:21.499
I don't think this is enough
to cover my labor costs.

33:21.582 --> 33:22.792
Come on, eat up.

33:23.501 --> 33:25.253
- Do you want a bottle of soju?
- Hmm.

33:25.336 --> 33:26.421
[phone ringing]

33:28.464 --> 33:30.508
[Sol-i] A bottle of soju, coming right up!

33:30.591 --> 33:32.093
Hi, this is Leezakaya.

33:32.719 --> 33:34.846
Yes. 6:30 p.m., for ten.

33:34.929 --> 33:36.055
What's your name?

33:36.848 --> 33:39.017
Yes. You wanna cancel?

33:40.268 --> 33:41.436
I see.

33:42.395 --> 33:43.688
It can't be helped.

33:44.397 --> 33:45.231
Okay.

33:47.025 --> 33:49.944
You know what?
I'm okay with paying for this.

33:50.028 --> 33:52.030
[awkward music]

33:52.113 --> 33:53.072
[dramatic sigh]

33:53.156 --> 33:55.533
[Sol-i] They're setting fire
to an already dying business!

33:55.616 --> 33:56.784
[screams]

33:57.702 --> 34:00.204
Why would they order octopus
if they're going to cancel?

34:00.788 --> 34:03.708
Excuse me, you got what happened, right?
Can you do me a favor?

34:04.208 --> 34:07.795
Please send a copy to one of those
whistle-blowing TV programs.

34:07.879 --> 34:09.881
[groans]
I'm stressed out.

34:11.632 --> 34:13.384
What'll I do with all the octopus?

34:14.343 --> 34:15.595
How about this.

34:15.678 --> 34:18.556
Let's try to get the customers
to order sliced, raw octopus.

34:18.639 --> 34:20.016
When they come, just serve that.

34:21.017 --> 34:22.977
Have you ever seen customers here?

34:23.978 --> 34:26.731
Well, once or twice, one or two…

34:30.276 --> 34:31.569
What else can I do?

34:32.236 --> 34:33.362
Eat and enjoy.

34:34.447 --> 34:37.158
You guys should take a break
and eat as much as you want to.

34:39.035 --> 34:40.203
[dramatic sigh]

34:42.246 --> 34:45.583
- Is there anyone you can call?
- Who? Me? What do you think?

34:45.666 --> 34:47.460
No wonder, 'cause I'm your only friend.

34:47.543 --> 34:48.419
What about you?

34:48.503 --> 34:53.132
I have a lot of ex-boyfriends.
But even so, you have only one of those.

34:54.675 --> 34:55.927
Excuse me.

34:57.470 --> 34:58.971
I know someone we could call.

34:59.055 --> 35:02.225
[hopeful music]

35:03.434 --> 35:06.062
SBC CURRENT AFFAIRS AND CULTURE
PRODUCER JUNG CHAE-RAN

35:08.481 --> 35:10.650
Hey. How's it going over there?

35:11.943 --> 35:12.819
Oh.

35:12.902 --> 35:14.362
- DON'T WALK, RUN RUNNING MAN
- I'll follow.

35:16.489 --> 35:18.282
Hmm. That sounds great.

35:18.366 --> 35:19.617
I'll head there when we're done.

35:20.409 --> 35:21.410
Okay.

35:23.996 --> 35:25.706
Hey, you're the intern, right?

35:25.790 --> 35:27.834
Yes, my name is Im Tae-hun.

35:27.917 --> 35:30.002
Go home and rest.
I'll wrap things up on my own.

35:30.086 --> 35:32.255
- No, wait--
- I don't like repeating myself. Take care.

35:34.841 --> 35:36.092
Sure, thanks a lot, sir!

35:39.345 --> 35:40.471
[thumping]

35:41.180 --> 35:43.432
Oh, my goodness. You guys are amazing.

35:43.516 --> 35:44.851
You really didn't have to do that.

35:44.934 --> 35:48.354
Don't worry, when the guests come here,
I will only charge them for the octopus.

35:48.437 --> 35:50.731
- Beer's free. On the house.
- Yeah, that's right.

35:50.815 --> 35:52.066
Come and have a drink with us.

35:52.150 --> 35:54.861
Come to think of it, we've never
had a meal together since we started.

35:54.944 --> 35:56.737
- Thanks, but I'm okay.
- Come on.

35:56.821 --> 35:58.823
Just turn off the camera and come here.

35:58.906 --> 36:00.700
I know. Do you guys…

36:00.783 --> 36:02.451
like octopus?

36:02.535 --> 36:05.079
- [Sol-i] Seriously? That little…
- Oh, sorry. I dropped everything.

36:05.163 --> 36:08.457
What are you doing, trying to feed
a grown-up and you end up making a mess?

36:09.041 --> 36:10.209
Welcome--

36:11.627 --> 36:12.628
Hang on.

36:13.337 --> 36:15.006
- You?
- [groans]

36:15.089 --> 36:16.966
It's… it's been a while.

36:18.634 --> 36:20.887
[gentle music]

36:22.555 --> 36:24.807
[Yeon-su] Meeting like this
threw me for a loop.

36:24.891 --> 36:26.434
It wasn't part of the plan.

36:29.103 --> 36:31.272
Hey. What brings you to this restaurant?

36:32.273 --> 36:33.983
We were told the shoot would be here.

36:35.234 --> 36:37.445
I came because
I heard there will be octopus.

36:39.488 --> 36:41.991
[sweet airy music]

36:43.201 --> 36:44.744
When I first met Choi Ung,

36:44.827 --> 36:47.455
I just started working part-time
at his father's restaurant.

36:47.538 --> 36:49.665
There was this unemployed guy
who always sat around

36:49.749 --> 36:51.250
on a wooden bench doing nothing.

36:51.334 --> 36:54.253
And that guy turned out to be their son.
That kid was the Ung master.

36:54.837 --> 36:57.298
So I approached him, even though
he had no idea of my presence--

36:57.381 --> 36:58.883
I can hear you.

36:58.966 --> 37:01.928
And at that moment, he started doodling
on these small pieces of paper.

37:02.011 --> 37:03.304
That's when, "Oh! I knew it."

37:03.387 --> 37:05.139
My animal instincts
were telling me this was it.

37:05.223 --> 37:07.433
I knew we could work together,
I could feel it.

37:07.516 --> 37:09.560
So when he became serious
about making it his career,

37:09.644 --> 37:11.354
I signed up to be his manager.

37:11.437 --> 37:14.982
[Eun-ho] That's why if you ask anybody,
they'll say I'm a diligent guy.

37:15.816 --> 37:17.860
I don't think anyone asked you.

37:17.944 --> 37:20.613
Anyway, since I've known him
the longest and I'm an old friend,

37:20.696 --> 37:22.615
you can ask me
anything you wanna know about him.

37:22.698 --> 37:23.908
What are you curious about?

37:23.991 --> 37:25.826
What should I tell you?
His job? Relationships?

37:25.910 --> 37:27.245
Hey, miss.

37:27.870 --> 37:29.372
You look familiar.
We've met before, right?

37:31.123 --> 37:32.625
- That's not going to work on me.
- [chuckles]

37:32.708 --> 37:35.086
- Of course, I'm sorry.
- [Sol-i] Here's your order.

37:35.169 --> 37:36.754
Hey, I'll just go to the bathroom, okay?

37:40.591 --> 37:41.717
Zoom in.

37:45.179 --> 37:48.766
[breathes heavily]

37:53.562 --> 37:56.732
[Yeon-su] So I guess,
I should apologize to him first, right?

37:57.316 --> 37:58.526
Okay.

37:58.609 --> 38:02.113
Since I'm the more mature person,
I should bring up the issue.

38:03.781 --> 38:06.158
- Listen, Ung, about yesterday--
- [Ung] I'm sorry.

38:06.242 --> 38:10.162
Last night I wasn't thinking straight.
Just forget about what I said.

38:10.246 --> 38:12.915
I was upset, and said some harsh things
I didn't really mean.

38:14.792 --> 38:15.793
Oh.

38:16.919 --> 38:18.754
Still, what I did was wrong.

38:18.838 --> 38:21.215
- So, I'm sorry about--
- [Ung] I know it wasn't your fault.

38:21.299 --> 38:22.300
So, it's okay.

38:23.801 --> 38:25.803
[soft music]

38:27.179 --> 38:28.014
Oh.

38:30.266 --> 38:33.686
My team, including the Soen Shop team,

38:33.769 --> 38:35.688
want to formally apologize to you.

38:35.771 --> 38:38.316
[Yeon-su] Another thing,
I'll return the project to the way it was

38:38.399 --> 38:39.442
- when we--
- I'll do it.

38:40.401 --> 38:42.862
- What?
- Yeah, I'm going to work with Nu-a.

38:45.573 --> 38:48.284
What? But why do that?

38:48.367 --> 38:50.161
There is no reason for me not to.

38:51.287 --> 38:53.581
Uh, that's true, but I mean…

38:53.664 --> 38:56.250
And you don't have to apologize.
I already met with him.

38:57.335 --> 38:59.378
- With whom?
- Mr. Jang, of course.

38:59.920 --> 39:02.798
- You met with him already? When?
- He called me earlier.

39:02.882 --> 39:05.593
Did he explain everything to you?
Did he apologize?

39:05.676 --> 39:08.012
What did he say?
And you, what did you say to him?

39:08.095 --> 39:09.930
Did you just brush it off again,
like you always do?

39:10.014 --> 39:12.850
You should tell him you were offended
and have him apologize for the--

39:12.933 --> 39:13.768
Enough.

39:16.103 --> 39:17.438
I'll take care of it.

39:18.022 --> 39:20.024
[soft music]

39:22.777 --> 39:23.861
[Yeon-su] How come…

39:24.737 --> 39:28.491
Choi Ung's acting
like a complete stranger today?

39:31.243 --> 39:32.203
Oh.

39:33.204 --> 39:34.330
Got it.

39:35.247 --> 39:39.085
So anyway, we only have
a week left until the big opening,

39:39.168 --> 39:41.128
so I'll make sure to prepare for it well.

39:42.171 --> 39:43.589
I'm sorry for being so childish.

39:44.423 --> 39:48.052
[Yeon-su] Of course, things are now going
the way they were supposed to.

39:48.135 --> 39:49.595
[Ung] As for the documentary…

39:50.554 --> 39:54.767
I agreed to shoot this for a month,
I'll do my best not to get distracted.

39:55.684 --> 39:57.353
Let's try to end this smoothly, shall we?

39:58.437 --> 40:00.314
[Yeon-su] What is this I'm feeling?

40:00.398 --> 40:01.524
Oh, no.

40:05.694 --> 40:08.781
Okay. If that's what you want,
let's do it.

40:09.865 --> 40:12.451
[soft music continues]

40:14.328 --> 40:17.498
Why do I feel like
there's something out of place?

40:25.589 --> 40:27.091
[mouse clicking]

40:27.591 --> 40:29.176
[creepy whooshing]

40:31.095 --> 40:32.888
[disappointed scared tune]

40:32.972 --> 40:34.348
What are you doing?

40:36.183 --> 40:39.270
At least pretend to be surprised.
You're such a killjoy.

40:40.563 --> 40:42.523
What are you doing here on a weekend?

40:42.606 --> 40:44.024
Hold on. Did you get a haircut?

40:44.608 --> 40:46.944
Your blind date, she canceled?

40:47.027 --> 40:49.155
- She said I wore a wig.
- Oh.

40:49.238 --> 40:51.157
What are you doing here at this hour?

40:51.240 --> 40:53.117
I'm making backup files
of what we shot today.

40:54.493 --> 40:58.038
Hey, I heard
Tae-jin made you fill in for him.

40:58.122 --> 41:00.791
- Why didn't he make Chae-ran do it?
- She was out doing fieldwork.

41:01.625 --> 41:04.837
That reminds me. I asked for
an additional team member, not an intern.

41:05.421 --> 41:07.173
If you're going to be picky,
then just send him back.

41:07.256 --> 41:09.925
Send him back?
Don't make him go from team to team.

41:10.509 --> 41:12.720
- Just have him work on my team.
- [Dong-il chuckles]

41:12.803 --> 41:15.431
You really are
more kindhearted than you look.

41:15.931 --> 41:17.141
[groans]

41:19.643 --> 41:21.145
So anyway, how's the shoot going?

41:21.729 --> 41:23.230
I haven't heard any updates
from you in a while.

41:23.314 --> 41:25.149
Why haven't you been sharing anything?

41:25.232 --> 41:27.359
There's nothing important
for me to share yet.

41:28.194 --> 41:30.070
Man, I wanna know what they're like.

41:30.154 --> 41:32.114
Wait, maybe I should go and watch.

41:33.032 --> 41:35.326
What about you? Are you having fun?

41:37.036 --> 41:38.245
I don't know…

41:39.330 --> 41:41.081
Maybe it's all a mistake.

41:42.166 --> 41:44.084
Excuse me, sir, is that fun?

41:44.168 --> 41:45.377
Hmm? What do you mean?

41:45.461 --> 41:47.129
Using a camera to film someone.

41:47.213 --> 41:49.048
- [indistinct chatter]
- [gasps]

41:49.632 --> 41:51.717
Oh, this? Yeah, it's fun.

41:51.800 --> 41:55.054
I guess looking into
other people's lives is fun.

41:55.137 --> 41:58.265
This way, you get to meet
all kinds of people all over the world,

41:58.349 --> 41:59.642
places you least expect.

42:00.184 --> 42:03.479
Watching makes you feel thankful
for your empty life.

42:04.980 --> 42:06.232
[Dong-il] Why?

42:06.315 --> 42:09.401
You really end up feeling
thankful for your empty life?

42:09.485 --> 42:12.238
[gentle music]

42:13.155 --> 42:14.156
What is it?

42:14.240 --> 42:17.117
I'm not going crazy or anything,
so stop looking at me like that.

42:17.201 --> 42:18.744
This is how I look.

42:18.827 --> 42:21.747
Just give it some time.
Before you know it, it'll be fun.

42:21.830 --> 42:24.792
Soon, you'll realize why
you're the person I selected for this job.

42:24.875 --> 42:26.377
[Ji-ung] Wasn't it
because I was available?

42:26.460 --> 42:27.962
How could you think that way?

42:28.045 --> 42:30.965
I can't believe you don't understand
your senior's good intentions.

42:31.465 --> 42:34.176
Figure out my intentions.
Homework. Got that?

42:34.260 --> 42:35.553
I'm heading out.

42:37.429 --> 42:38.847
[Ji-ung] Are you drunk or something?

42:39.723 --> 42:41.976
[gentle music continues]

42:44.770 --> 42:45.729
Here.

42:46.397 --> 42:48.065
- It's on the house.
- [gasps]

42:48.148 --> 42:50.651
Those are fresh clams.
By the way, I made a stew out of it.

42:50.734 --> 42:53.320
It's on the house
since I haven't seen you in a long time.

42:53.862 --> 42:56.407
You're looking good. How long has it been?

42:56.490 --> 42:57.658
After you two broke up…

42:59.410 --> 43:03.247
I meant, the last time we saw each other
was our graduation.

43:03.330 --> 43:04.540
It's been a while, right?

43:04.623 --> 43:06.750
- [chopsticks clink]
- You're right. It has been a while.

43:06.834 --> 43:09.044
I heard you're not so bad as an artist.

43:09.128 --> 43:11.422
Not at all. In fact, he's doing great!

43:11.505 --> 43:13.215
He's kicking ass these days, right?

43:14.341 --> 43:17.803
Well, I remember you used to draw a lot.
Is that why you're successful?

43:17.886 --> 43:20.264
Oh, yeah. He's killing it out there
with his drawings.

43:20.347 --> 43:22.266
Even Yeon-su, of all people,
came to ask him

43:22.766 --> 43:24.560
if he could work with them
on some projects.

43:24.643 --> 43:25.686
[Eun-ho] Need I say more?

43:25.769 --> 43:27.938
You really don't know
what's gonna happen in the future.

43:28.022 --> 43:31.233
Who would have thought
that things would be like this now,

43:31.317 --> 43:33.277
after you and Ung
put an end to your relationship.

43:34.695 --> 43:37.865
[awkward strumming]

43:38.699 --> 43:40.993
- I'm gonna go and get some air.
- Yes, let's go.

43:41.076 --> 43:42.536
Do you smoke by any chance?

43:42.620 --> 43:44.788
- No, but I'm still going outside.
- Me neither, but let's go.

43:45.789 --> 43:48.751
- [Sol-i] Let's go. You're confused.
- [Ung sighs]

43:50.127 --> 43:51.295
[sighs]

43:51.378 --> 43:54.381
Those two are unbelievable,
they mess up every time.

43:55.257 --> 43:57.551
[Ung] Hmm.

44:00.220 --> 44:03.515
[Yeon-su] Why is he like this?
He's acting so cold.

44:04.892 --> 44:06.393
What else did you wanna ask me?

44:06.477 --> 44:09.605
[Yeon-su] Is he like this
because he's mad at me? Or maybe…

44:09.688 --> 44:11.273
You went through a lot in the first video

44:11.357 --> 44:14.234
and the public will see you
meeting again after ten long years.

44:14.318 --> 44:15.736
How do you feel about that?

44:16.403 --> 44:17.571
[Ung] It was a long time ago,

44:17.655 --> 44:19.865
so I had forgotten
some parts of the documentary,

44:20.449 --> 44:23.077
but it was actually nice
to see each other again.

44:23.952 --> 44:26.955
If you saw the video, then you know
that we're not exactly friends.

44:27.039 --> 44:29.124
[soft music]

44:30.959 --> 44:33.003
[Yeon-su] Is he really
okay with everything?

44:34.171 --> 44:35.172
[Chae-ran] Yeon-su.

44:36.715 --> 44:37.800
Hey, Yeon-su.

44:38.592 --> 44:40.719
- [Yeon-su] Yes?
- How do you feel about this?

44:40.803 --> 44:41.720
Oh…

44:42.846 --> 44:44.890
It was pretty much the same for me.

44:44.973 --> 44:47.434
I was happy
and surprised to see him again.

44:48.477 --> 44:50.479
[soft pensive music]

45:01.156 --> 45:02.241
[sighs]

45:06.161 --> 45:07.663
[deep sigh]

45:09.081 --> 45:11.166
[crickets creaking]

45:15.295 --> 45:16.338
[music stops]

45:21.885 --> 45:23.762
- Good, you're here.
- Hi, good morning, Ms. Kook.

45:24.346 --> 45:26.598
Ms. Kook, Go-oh sent us
a proposal this morning

45:26.682 --> 45:28.392
regarding the collaboration show.

45:28.475 --> 45:30.436
It's on our drive,
please check it as soon as possible.

45:30.519 --> 45:32.146
- Sure.
- But nothing yet from Nu-a.

45:32.229 --> 45:34.356
Got it. We'll have the meeting
after I check the reports.

45:34.440 --> 45:36.233
- [Myeong-ho] Sure, no problem.
- Okay.

45:36.316 --> 45:37.818
100 HOURS OF WORK
5 HOURS OF LIVE DRAWING

45:38.861 --> 45:40.404
A hundred hours?

45:40.487 --> 45:43.407
[Ye-in] Is he really serious about
going to work for one hundred hours?

45:43.490 --> 45:44.950
[Myeong-ho] Hard to believe, right?

45:45.033 --> 45:47.995
I think he's going to show us
his work process for the very first time.

45:48.078 --> 45:50.080
He says he's going
to record the whole thing

45:50.164 --> 45:51.665
from the time he starts
until he finishes his piece.

45:52.249 --> 45:55.002
Can he do that in five days? Oh, my.

45:55.085 --> 45:57.087
[Myeong-ho] He said
he's going to work for five straight days

45:57.171 --> 46:00.048
and draw the rest in front of an audience
on the day of the opening.

46:00.132 --> 46:02.384
[sighs]
Is that even humanly possible?

46:03.093 --> 46:05.929
So aside from the time he eats and sleeps,

46:06.013 --> 46:07.848
he's going to be drawing
for 19 hours a day?

46:07.931 --> 46:10.184
- [Myeong-ho] Something like that.
- [gasps]

46:10.267 --> 46:12.227
He's a far greater artist
than I gave him credit for.

46:19.067 --> 46:21.695
Make sure everything is set up early,
so we can start smoothly.

46:22.279 --> 46:24.573
Please make sure to check everything
thoroughly at the scene.

46:24.656 --> 46:27.117
And you can take care of this.
I know you've got this.

46:27.201 --> 46:29.411
[uplifting music]

46:30.370 --> 46:32.623
The main event
of the opening ceremony will be

46:32.706 --> 46:35.501
the live drawing show of the artists
as well as the closing.

46:35.584 --> 46:38.128
Next, I'd like to go
over the details of the event.

46:38.212 --> 46:39.963
After the cake cutting ceremony,

46:40.547 --> 46:42.883
we're going to take
a group photo for the press.

46:42.966 --> 46:45.844
[Eun-ho] Yes, we finished this.
And we're working on that right now.

46:46.887 --> 46:48.931
We'll put one camera on top
and one on the side.

46:49.431 --> 46:50.432
I'll let you know once we're set.

46:50.516 --> 46:52.893
- [man] Okay, thank you.
- [Eun-ho] Yeah, no problem at all.

46:56.355 --> 46:58.357
[uplifting music continues]

46:59.483 --> 47:02.069
I'm sorry, I'm gonna have
to call you back, okay?

47:02.736 --> 47:04.613
Yes, give me just, maybe ten minutes.

47:06.156 --> 47:08.242
[uplifting music]

47:21.004 --> 47:23.048
[uplifting music continues]

47:32.599 --> 47:35.185
As you can see, the sign says Gamjatang.

47:35.269 --> 47:36.478
Yes, that is correct.

47:36.562 --> 47:39.273
We weren't really trying to
run a business when we started in this--

47:39.356 --> 47:41.233
Come on, let's have
some gamjatang for dinner.

47:41.316 --> 47:44.152
It's something our family
used to enjoy for so long.

47:44.236 --> 47:46.113
[Ho] Here's the chicken feet restaurant.
This way.

47:46.196 --> 47:49.491
- There's a seafood stew restaurant here.
- [Chang-sik] He's really excited.

47:53.704 --> 47:54.913
[gasps]
Welcome back, sir.

47:54.997 --> 47:57.457
- Hello, a table for two, please.
- Did you just get off work?

47:57.541 --> 47:59.084
- Yeah.
- Let me know when you're ready to order.

47:59.167 --> 48:00.294
[man] Okay.

48:00.377 --> 48:02.671
Thanks for coming.
Hope you enjoyed the food.

48:02.754 --> 48:04.840
- [man] We're definitely coming back.
- [Sol-i] Thank you.

48:08.468 --> 48:10.887
["Christmas Tree" by V playing]

48:14.558 --> 48:18.061
♪ In this moment ♪

48:18.145 --> 48:20.731
♪ I see you ♪

48:21.648 --> 48:26.486
♪ It always comes around as I believed ♪

48:28.196 --> 48:31.783
♪ When the rain stops ♪

48:31.867 --> 48:34.786
♪ You shine on me ♪

48:35.495 --> 48:40.792
♪ Your light's the only thing
That keeps the cold out ♪

48:41.418 --> 48:45.005
♪ Moon in the summer night ♪

48:45.088 --> 48:48.008
♪ Whispering of the stars ♪

48:48.091 --> 48:49.760
♪ They're singing like ♪

48:49.843 --> 48:53.847
♪ Christmas trees for us ♪

48:55.182 --> 48:57.893
♪ So I'll tell you ♪

48:57.976 --> 49:01.313
♪ A million tiny things that ♪

49:01.396 --> 49:05.067
♪ You have never known ♪

49:05.150 --> 49:08.862
♪ It all gets tangled up inside ♪

49:08.945 --> 49:11.531
♪ And I'll tell you ♪

49:11.615 --> 49:15.118
♪ A million little reasons ♪

49:15.202 --> 49:18.372
♪ I'm falling for your eyes ♪

49:19.039 --> 49:23.502
♪ I just want to be where you are ♪

49:24.544 --> 49:27.714
♪ It's such a strange thing to do ♪

49:27.798 --> 49:31.051
♪ Sometimes I don't understand you ♪

49:31.134 --> 49:34.721
♪ But it always brings me back ♪

49:35.681 --> 49:38.725
- ♪ To where you are ♪
- [Ung sighs]

49:47.317 --> 49:49.736
[instrumental music]

49:52.406 --> 49:53.782
[deep breath]

50:00.914 --> 50:01.915
Hi, grandma, I'm home.

50:02.499 --> 50:04.167
You must be tired. Go.

50:04.251 --> 50:05.419
[both chuckle]

50:15.429 --> 50:16.388
[sighs]

50:33.989 --> 50:37.033
CHOI UNG

50:43.582 --> 50:44.583
[sighs]

50:45.208 --> 50:48.712
We can't take any more chances,
so make sure to expose more than enough.

50:48.795 --> 50:50.547
- Yes.
- What do you think of this space?

50:50.630 --> 50:51.840
You think it'd be enough for the show?

50:51.923 --> 50:54.551
I'll make sure this entire space
gets in the shot, Mr. Jang.

50:54.634 --> 50:55.761
All right. Moving on.

50:57.721 --> 50:59.973
[slow smooth music]

51:07.105 --> 51:09.107
[smooth music continues]

51:23.830 --> 51:24.664
Hi, Ms. Kook.

51:27.667 --> 51:29.878
- [Ye-in] Ms. Kook?
- [gasps]

51:29.961 --> 51:31.254
Hi, Ye-in.

51:31.338 --> 51:33.673
You should go home and get some rest.
You have a big day tomorrow.

51:33.757 --> 51:36.676
You should go get some rest too.
You did good today.

51:38.637 --> 51:40.889
Oh, by the way…

51:40.972 --> 51:43.350
How much do you think
Go-oh has done so far?

51:43.433 --> 51:45.435
Do you think he made it to 100 hours?

51:46.228 --> 51:49.064
Well, I'm sure he did fine.

51:49.648 --> 51:53.819
Hmm. I bet he's been working so hard
that he hasn't been able to sleep or eat.

51:54.694 --> 51:56.363
Being an artist is hard work.

51:57.030 --> 51:58.907
'Kay, I'm going now. Take care.

52:03.411 --> 52:06.164
["Drawer" by 10CM playing]

52:14.965 --> 52:16.341
GU EUN-HO

52:18.426 --> 52:21.137
[operator] The person you are trying
to reach is unavailable right now.

52:21.221 --> 52:23.890
Please leave a message
after the tone. Thank you.

52:26.476 --> 52:28.186
KIM JI-UNG

52:31.398 --> 52:32.691
[Ji-ung] Hey, what's going on?

52:32.774 --> 52:34.943
Hey, Ji-ung.
[chuckles awkwardly]

52:35.777 --> 52:38.905
How is Ung doing? Was he okay?

52:38.989 --> 52:41.700
[Ji-ung] Yes. He was still alive
the last time I saw him at his studio.

52:41.783 --> 52:43.702
Oh, I see.

52:44.369 --> 52:46.538
[Ji-ung] If you're that worried,
give him a call.

52:46.621 --> 52:47.998
Uh, no, that's okay.

52:49.124 --> 52:51.877
But Eun-ho is with Ung anyway, isn't he?

52:51.960 --> 52:54.129
No, he's not. Eun-ho left earlier with me.

52:54.713 --> 52:56.464
[Ji-ung] Ung said
he'll finish up by himself.

52:56.548 --> 52:57.841
Will he be okay alone?

52:57.924 --> 52:59.175
[Ji-ung] He's not gonna die.

52:59.259 --> 53:02.178
Oh, right, you don't know.
He usually works like that.

53:02.971 --> 53:03.972
I see.

53:05.849 --> 53:07.100
Okay then.

53:07.183 --> 53:09.603
Wait. You're coming tomorrow, right?

53:10.854 --> 53:13.064
Hmm. Yeah. See you then.

53:18.278 --> 53:20.530
["Drawer" by 10CM continues]

53:37.631 --> 53:40.425
- [heartbeat thumping]
- [groans]

53:44.971 --> 53:46.056
[sighs]

53:47.098 --> 53:48.016
[pen clinks]

53:51.937 --> 53:53.647
- [sighs]
- [thuds]

54:02.405 --> 54:03.615
[groans]

54:07.744 --> 54:08.578
GO-OH'S 100 HOURS

54:08.662 --> 54:09.663
EVENT OUTLINE

54:13.667 --> 54:14.793
[music stops]

54:20.382 --> 54:22.467
If I call him right now
to ask about the event,

54:22.550 --> 54:24.094
it's not going to be weird, right?

54:24.177 --> 54:25.178
I'll just check on him.

54:28.223 --> 54:29.391
[sighs]

54:30.558 --> 54:34.062
Nah, Ung's super sensitive,
he might just go crazy on me.

54:35.063 --> 54:38.400
I mean, seriously. Can't he just
check in and call me from time to time

54:38.483 --> 54:40.360
to give me an update on his progress?

54:41.444 --> 54:43.613
Gosh, he can be so frustrating.

54:43.697 --> 54:47.117
[groaning sigh]
Why do I care anyway?

54:48.284 --> 54:49.661
I'm don't care anymore.

54:50.620 --> 54:52.664
[light cheeky music]

54:53.373 --> 54:54.624
[sighs]

55:00.338 --> 55:03.633
[Yeon-su] I don't know
what I'm doing here at his place.

55:04.676 --> 55:06.720
[crickets creaking]

55:10.223 --> 55:11.474
No, I can't!

55:11.558 --> 55:15.145
Checking on the artist who's the
most important part for tomorrow's event

55:15.228 --> 55:17.272
is something that's absolutely necessary.

55:22.360 --> 55:24.154
Even if the artist wasn't Choi Ung,

55:24.237 --> 55:26.489
- I would have done this exact same thing.
- [bell dings]

55:26.573 --> 55:29.159
Scratch that.
I would have cared for them even more. 

55:29.242 --> 55:32.829
That's right. It's just purely business.
That's the reason why I came tonight.

55:34.748 --> 55:36.833
[cheeky awkward music]

55:48.928 --> 55:50.221
[knocking]

55:55.810 --> 55:56.978
[knocking louder]

56:12.660 --> 56:14.162
[Yeon-su] Oh.

56:17.457 --> 56:20.335
I rang the bell, but you didn't answer
so I was calling you.

56:25.131 --> 56:27.342
I didn't come here to interrupt you.

56:27.425 --> 56:30.762
I was going over the event details
and came to check on you…

56:30.845 --> 56:34.641
I mean, checking on the artist
is part of my job, you know.

56:35.517 --> 56:37.519
My boss told me to check on you.

56:37.602 --> 56:39.437
[light awkward music]

56:41.314 --> 56:44.400
This is jujube.
You have a hard time sleeping…

56:44.484 --> 56:47.487
What I mean is,
you're working so I was told to give this.

56:48.738 --> 56:50.782
Have some tea and get some sleep.

56:51.908 --> 56:53.701
It's been 95 hours.

56:54.661 --> 56:55.912
Hmm?

56:57.372 --> 56:59.916
I just finished working for 95 hours.

57:01.126 --> 57:03.962
I'll draw the rest
in front of the audience tomorrow.

57:04.671 --> 57:06.089
For real?

57:06.714 --> 57:08.299
You really did all that work?

57:09.008 --> 57:11.469
[chuckles softly]
You're so amazing.

57:14.722 --> 57:17.767
Anyway, drink this so you can sleep.

57:24.524 --> 57:27.444
[Yeon-su] See? This wasn't so bad at all.

57:28.319 --> 57:29.612
I'm gonna go now.

57:30.280 --> 57:33.241
Things are neat and very professional.

57:38.163 --> 57:39.330
And then…

57:45.879 --> 57:47.005
Can you stay over?

57:49.132 --> 57:50.925
["Maybe If" by BIBI playing]

57:51.718 --> 57:54.262
♪ Maybe if I ♪

57:55.638 --> 57:58.683
♪ Woke up in the morning ♪

57:59.309 --> 58:02.187
♪ Hearing your voice ♪

58:02.729 --> 58:06.608
♪ Maybe if I was with you ♪

58:07.567 --> 58:13.573
EPILOGUE

58:16.868 --> 58:18.077
I'll do it.

58:18.661 --> 58:21.039
I don't care if I do it
with Nu-a or with someone else.

58:23.708 --> 58:26.211
Smart decision.
You are wiser than I thought.

58:27.295 --> 58:29.172
Then we'll proceed like we've discussed.

58:31.049 --> 58:33.176
And I apologize
for what happened that day.

58:34.302 --> 58:37.722
No, don't. It's fine.
I was on edge that day as well.

58:38.348 --> 58:40.391
So I'd also like to apologize.

58:40.475 --> 58:42.977
You were really upset
at Yeon-su, not at me.

58:52.445 --> 58:53.530
Uh…

58:54.489 --> 58:56.324
Can I ask you a personal question?

58:57.367 --> 58:59.118
I'm not sure I like the idea of that,

58:59.202 --> 59:01.412
but since you are asking,
sure. What is it?

59:08.795 --> 59:10.547
Never mind.
[clears throat]

59:15.343 --> 59:17.512
You know, you're very easy
to read, Mr. Choi.

59:19.889 --> 59:22.308
At the event,
when you were looking at Yeon-su,

59:22.892 --> 59:25.436
it was obvious to me
you hadn't gotten over her yet.

59:26.854 --> 59:28.523
Uh. What are you talking about?

59:28.606 --> 59:30.316
I think everyone knows except you.

59:31.192 --> 59:34.320
As long as you don't screw up this project
because of your personal feelings,

59:34.404 --> 59:36.197
I really couldn't care less.

59:36.281 --> 59:39.534
And of course, Yeon-su assured me
that it's over between you two.

59:41.286 --> 59:42.120
She told you that?

59:43.288 --> 59:45.290
As for my answer to your question…

59:48.376 --> 59:52.005
Mr. Choi Ung, Yeon-su is very talented.

59:53.798 --> 59:55.383
And that's why I like her.

59:57.844 --> 01:00:00.555
Of course,
just nothing more than a partner.

01:00:00.638 --> 01:00:02.265
I think for that question…

01:00:03.516 --> 01:00:06.227
you should be asking somebody else,
because you've got the wrong guy.

01:00:06.853 --> 01:00:09.188
[Yeon-su] Wait.
You're coming tomorrow, right?

01:00:09.272 --> 01:00:11.149
- Yeah, see you then.
- Yeah.

01:00:12.150 --> 01:00:14.152
[soft light music]

01:00:26.664 --> 01:00:28.666
DELETE

01:00:35.757 --> 01:00:42.764
A SECRET THAT CAN'T BE TOLD

01:01:04.118 --> 01:01:07.038
[Yeon-su] What should I tell him
if he brings up last night?

01:01:07.872 --> 01:01:11.209
[Ung] I think I finally appreciate
Yeon-su for who she is.

01:01:11.292 --> 01:01:13.878
[Nu-a] We've got another artist
who'll be drawing in the next room.

01:01:13.961 --> 01:01:16.547
But I think,
you'll be too captivated to go there.

01:01:16.631 --> 01:01:20.093
[Yeon-su] I saw this look in Ung's eyes
as he was drawing today.

01:01:20.176 --> 01:01:22.553
It felt like
he was finally baring his soul.

01:01:22.637 --> 01:01:24.389
I haven't seen this side of you before.

01:01:24.472 --> 01:01:26.724
Hey. You still like him, don't you?
